      <section class="reveal define" id="what-is-magelift">
        <h2>What is MageLift?</h2>
        <p>
          MageLift is an open-source CLI and YAML config for Magento Open Source
          and Adobe Commerce in <strong>your</strong> AWS or GCP account. The YAML
          shape will feel familiar if you have used ACC or Upsun. Production support
          today covers AWS ECS Fargate and GCP GKE Autopilot.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="reveal audience">
        <div>
          <h2>Who it is for</h2>
          <p>
            Agencies with several Magento shops, and smaller teams without a
            dedicated DevOps hire, who want Magento-shaped YAML instead of an empty
            Terraform or Pulumi repo.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Familiar config</strong>
            <span><code>magelift.yaml</code> follows ACC/Upsun habits Magento people already know.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your invoice</strong>
            <span>Compute and data stay in your cloud. MageLift is the CLI, not a reseller.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Destroyable previews</strong>
            <span>Spin a preview, share a URL, tear it down. Protected destroys need <code>--yes</code>.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Certified vs experimental</strong>
            <span>Only certified cells are production-supported. Experimental stays labeled.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="reveal">
        <h2>From install to preview</h2>
        <p>
          Certified path today: AWS ECS Fargate and GCP GKE Autopilot. Prefer
          free-tier-safe shapes until you mean to spend.
        </p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <span>Install with <code>go install</code> until the first release tag,
            then prefer a release archive. Run <code>magelift version</code>.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>Copy <code>examples/sample-shop/magelift.yaml</code>, fill account
            and secret refs, then <code>magelift config validate</code>.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>Bootstrap once, then <code>preview</code> / <code>deploy</code> on a
            certified target. Destroy when the spike is done.</span>
          </li>
        </ol>
